question_text:
Rationalize the denominator:

\[ `\boxed{
\frac{16x^2-y^2}{2\sqrt{x}-\sqrt{y}}
}`{=tex} \]

Simplify the following expression:

\[ `\boxed{
\frac{
(3x+2)^{1/2}(2x+3)^{-2/3}
-
(2x+3)^{1/3}(3x+2)^{-1/2}
}{
3x+2
}
}`{=tex} \]

Express as a sum of terms of the form (ax\^r), where (a) is a real
number and (r) is a rational number:

\[ `\boxed{
\frac{(\sqrt{x}-3)^2}{x^3}
}`{=tex} \]

Solve the equation:

\[ `\boxed{
\frac{3}{7x-2}
=
\frac{9}{3x+1}
}`{=tex} \]

Solve for (x) in terms of (y):

\[ `\boxed{
4x^2-4xy+1-y^2=0
}`{=tex} \]

Write as a single number of the form

\[ a+bi \]

with (a) and (b) real:

\[ `\boxed{
\frac{-3-2i}{5+2i}
}`{=tex} \]

Find all real values of (x) and (y) satisfying

\[ `\boxed{
(x-y)+3i=7+yi
}`{=tex} \]

The volume of a sphere of radius (r) is

\[ `\boxed{
V=\frac{4\pi r^3}{3}
}`{=tex}. \]

A meteorologist is inflating a spherical balloon with helium gas.

If the radius of the balloon is changing at a rate of

\[ 1.5`\text{ cm/sec}`{=tex}, \]

express the volume (V) of the balloon as a function of time (t), in
seconds.

\[ `\boxed{
\log_a\left(\frac{x}{y}\right)
=
\log_a(x)-\log_a(y)
}`{=tex} \]

\[ `\boxed{
\log_a(x^n)=n\log_a(x)
}`{=tex} \]

The notes specify

\[ x,y\>0 \]

and real values of (n).

Simplify:

\[ `\boxed{
\left[\frac{x-2y}{5z+1}\right]
\div
\left[\frac{3x-6y}{-z-(2+9z)}\right]
}`{=tex} \]

Simplify, where (a) and (b) can be any real numbers:

\[ `\boxed{
\frac{\sqrt{a^4b^6}}
{\sqrt{a^{12}b^8}}
}`{=tex} \]

Simplify:

\[ `\boxed{
\frac{x^3-2x^2}
{x^2-3x-10}
}`{=tex} \]

Simplify:

\[ `\boxed{
\frac1{x+1}
-
\frac1{x+2}
+
\frac3{(x+1)(x+2)}
}`{=tex} \]

\[ `\frac{x^3-2x^2}`{=tex} {x\^2-3x-10}. \]

Factor the numerator:

\[ x^3-2x^2=x\^2(x-2). \]

Factor the denominator:

\[ x\^2-3x-10 = x\^2-5x+2x-10 \]

\[ =x(x-5)+2(x-5) \]

\[ =(x+2)(x-5). \]

Thus

\[ `\boxed{
\frac{x^2(x-2)}
{(x+2)(x-5)}
}`{=tex} \]

with no common factor to cancel.

General midpoint formula: \[ `\boxed{
MP=\left(\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\frac{y_1+y_2}{2}\right)
}`{=tex}. \]

For \[ A(-1,7),`\qquad `{=tex}B(5,3): \]

\[ MP = `\left`{=tex}( `\frac{-1+5}{2}`{=tex}, `\frac{7+3}{2}`{=tex}
`\right`{=tex}) \]

\[ `\boxed{MP=(2,5)}`{=tex}. \]

The graph on page 3 shows:

-   a closed point at ((-3,-4));
-   an open point at ((-1,-2)) on the increasing segment;
-   a closed point at ((-1,1)) on the decreasing segment;
-   an open point at ((2,-2)).

Simplify: \[ `\boxed{
\left(\frac{a^2a^5}{b^{-2}}\right)^2b^4
}`{=tex} \]

Simplify, where (a,b) may be any real numbers: \[ `\boxed{
\sqrt{a^3b^2}\,\sqrt{a^7b^4}
}`{=tex} \]

Simplify and rationalize the denominator: \[ `\boxed{
\frac{x^2y}{\sqrt[3]{y^5}}
}`{=tex} \]

Rationalize the numerator: \[ `\boxed{
\frac{5+\sqrt{x}}{5-\sqrt{x}}
}`{=tex} \]

Simplify and fully factor the numerator and denominator: \[ `\boxed{
\frac3{x-2}-\frac6{x^2+x-6}
}`{=tex} \]

Simplify and fully factor: \[ `\boxed{
\frac{-2x^2+14x-20}{x-2}
\div
\frac{x^2-25}{3x}
}`{=tex} \]

Solve: \[ `\boxed{
\frac{x(x-2)}{x+3}<0
}`{=tex}. \]

Write the answer in interval notation.

Simplify and then rationalize the denominator: \[ `\boxed{
\frac{\sqrt[5]{8x^3y^4}}
{\sqrt[5]{4x^4y^2}}
}`{=tex} \]

Rationalize the numerator: \[ `\boxed{
\frac{\sqrt{x}}
{\sqrt[5]{y^3}}
}`{=tex} \]

> The source page is visually typeset; this transcription preserves the
> readable radical structure visible in the review.

Simplify into one rational expression: \[ `\boxed{
\frac{t}{t+3}
+
\frac{4t}{t-3}
-
\frac{18}{t^2-9}
}`{=tex} \]

Rationalize the denominator: \[ `\boxed{
\frac{\sqrt{t}-4}{\sqrt{t}+4}
}`{=tex} \]

Simplify \[ `\boxed{
\frac{1-7i}{6-2i}
}`{=tex} \] into a single complex number of the form \[ a+bi, \] where
(a,b) are real.

Find all real numbers (x,y) satisfying \[ `\boxed{
8+(3x+y)i=2x-4i
}`{=tex}. \]

Find all real numbers satisfying \[ `\boxed{
6u^{-1/2}-13u^{-1/4}+6=0
}`{=tex}. \]

Find all real numbers satisfying \[ `\boxed{
\frac{x^2-x-2}{x^2+4x+3}\ge0
}`{=tex}. \]

\[ `\frac{x^2y}{\sqrt[3]{y^5}}`{=tex} =
`\frac{x^2}{\sqrt[3]{y^2}}`{=tex}. \]

Multiply numerator and denominator by (`\sqrt[3]{y}`{=tex}): \[ `\boxed{
\frac{x^2\sqrt[3]{y}}{y}
}`{=tex}. \]
